{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjaJQC5oFKSe1jk25Lxa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R3Da3sCxtHBQ3GN2gtnzmL","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"working":"The line opens with a double barline and a 'dolce'-like marking above the staff. The first bar is edition bar 23. It has a dotted-8th G5 above the top line beamed to a 16th Eb5 in the top space. Then comes a quarter F5 on the top line. Last is a quarter double stop, D5 on the fourth line with D4 below the staff. A single barline follows. The second bar is edition bar 24: a dotted-half double stop, Eb5 in the top space and Eb4 in the bottom space, with a fermata over it. At the right edge there is a double bar with what look like repeat dots or a section mark. That fits the section change before bar 25 ('Sciolte', 'a mezza voce'). None of bar 25's 16th-note run is on this line. One mismatch: the edition has [f] at bar 23, but the copy shows a 'dolce'-like word there. That is a marking difference only. Pitches and rhythm match.","right":true,"insights":"The line was easy to match because it is short and distinctive. The rhythm is dotted 8th, 16th, quarter, then a quarter double stop. A dotted-half double stop with a fermata follows, and the line ends at a section break. The doubtful parts were the dynamic word, which differs from the edition's [f], and the cut-off sign at the right edge. A slightly wider crop would have shown whether that sign is a repeat."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4998,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4998},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":